config SECURITY_PRESSURE
	bool "Pressure Provenance, Secret UID, Device & Encrypted FD LSM"
	depends on SECURITY && SECURITYFS && NET && INET
	default y
	help
	  Enables the Pressure Linux Security Module providing:
	  - Non-monotonic randomized 31-bit Feistel-encrypted public FDs
	    mapped to randomized private fdtable slots
	  - 3-strike violation audit logging and uncatchable SIGKILL
	  - Public/secret kernel user & daemon UID mappings with pressure-authd
	  - Universal /dev & net_device cryptographic IDs and seat exclusivity
	  - Universal LOCAL vs. REMOTE provenance and event confinement
